From: GloriousEggroll <gloriouseggroll@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dxgi: Enable fullscreen focus-loss compatibility for Black Desert.

The matching Wine patch filters Black Desert's fullscreen deactivation
notifications without retaining actual foreground or input focus.
DXGI must also refrain from independently leaving fullscreen after its
100 ms foreground-loss check.

Enable the existing dxgi.keepFullscreenOnFocusLoss option only for
blackdesert64.exe, including case variants and non-Steam installations.
Keep the FFXIV profile and the option's implementation unchanged.
This profile alone does not prevent the game's own windowed-mode switch.

Apply after dxgi-keep-fullscreen-on-focus-loss.patch and pair with
patches/game-patches/black-desert-keep-fullscreen-on-focus-loss.patch.
Runtime verification of the combined behavior is pending.

Issue: https://github.com/GloriousEggroll/proton-ge-custom/issues/721

---
diff --git a/dxvk.conf b/dxvk.conf
--- a/dxvk.conf
+++ b/dxvk.conf
@@ -78,7 +78,8 @@
 # restore from dropping Wine's fullscreen upscaling. Focus and input still
 # belong to the newly activated window.
 # Explicit fullscreen/windowed requests and minimized-window handling remain
-# unchanged. This does not affect D3D9 and is enabled by default for FFXIV.
+# unchanged. This does not affect D3D9. Enabled by default for FFXIV and
+# Black Desert, which also needs Wine's application-deactivation fix.
 #
 # Supported values: True, False
 
diff --git a/src/util/config/config.cpp b/src/util/config/config.cpp
--- a/src/util/config/config.cpp
+++ b/src/util/config/config.cpp
@@ -483,6 +483,11 @@
     { R"(\\LEGOLCUR_DX11\.exe$)", {{
       { "d3d11.disableDirectImageMapping",  "True" },
     }} },
+    /* Black Desert: Wine preserves fullscreen on application deactivation.
+     * Do not independently leave it again when DXGI detects foreground loss. */
+    { R"(\\blackdesert64\.exe$)", {{
+      { "dxgi.keepFullscreenOnFocusLoss",   "True" },
+    }} },
     /* Wargame: European Escalation: Broken gamma   *
      * ramp when nvapi is available for some reason */
     { R"(\\Wargame European Escalation\\WarGame\.exe$)", {{
